{
 "what": "Master Version 2.67 — the audit-flags + set-type review edit, 243 cells, nothing added or removed. (1) 88 rows added by the Office / crawls since Oct 18 with a BLANK Item Type get a type from their own words, in the word their tab already uses (K-Line O 58, RMT O 23, Lionel MPC-Modern 4, Williams O 2, Micro-Trains N 1). (2) 46 new Lionel Pre-War variation rows with a blank Gauge get their parent row's gauge (Standard & O; 127 Standard). (3) 48 other-maker rows typed as an engine whose product is a set: unit-only sets → Diesel Set / Electric Set, engine-plus-cars or named sets → Set (Marx 4222 → Set; Lionel PW 4681 and Williams BERK115 / HDO27-1 kept). (4) 57 MTH rows checked against mthtrains.com: 28 RDC Budd Car Sets → Set, 22 → Set, 6 → Diesel Set, 22-90935 → Tank Car (18 kept: turbines with tenders, C-Liner A units, 20-2595B). (5) Kato N 106-4801 / 106-4802 Set → Tank Car (car packs are the car they hold, as their sisters 106-4803..4806). (6) American Models S 3220 → Hopper, 6027 → Flatcar (typed Steam Locomotive by mistake at 2.65). Not in this record: the 4 pre-war years on PW - Science / PW - Other (left as they are) and the 30 RMT \"Part\" rows (an app change, next release).",
